<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-US well flow sparks First Aust shares.</title>
<headline>RTRS-US well flow sparks First Aust shares.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in oil and gas explorer, First Australian Resources NL rocketed 46 percent to 38 cents after the company announced promising results from its South Louisiana well in the US.</p>
<p>Brokers said investors' interest had been piqued as First Australian was the only Australian-listed exposure to the field. The company said State Lease 3258's Number One well at South Lake Raccouri in south Louisiana had been perforated between 15,509 feet and 15,520 feet and had flow tested at a rate of 5.26 million cubic feet of gas and 687 barrels of oil per day.</p>
</text>
